[list]
[*]A stand no longer leaves a colonist without basic clothing. If what it hands out does not cover them, whatever they are wearing underneath stays on instead of going into the stand. The innermost layers are the ones kept, so a shirt and trousers stay put while a parka or a duster goes into storage as normal.
[*]This shows up most with Change the whole outfit ticked. That setting takes off everything the colonist arrived in, so a stand holding only a hat, a belt or a pair of trousers used to send them out with nothing else on. They now keep what they need and the rest of the swap happens as before. Everything else about the setting is unchanged.
[*]Whether anything is held back depends on the colonist. RimWorld asks for trousers on everyone and a covered torso as well on women, so the same stand with the same setting can keep a shirt on one colonist and not on another. Nothing is held back when the stand's own kit already covers them.
[*]A colonist who is already without basic clothing is still dressed by a stand as normal. Nothing was taken from them, so there is nothing to hold back.
[*]Nudists are exempt, and so is anyone whose ideoligion prefers nudity. For them being dressed is the penalty, so nothing is held back and the stand does exactly what it was set to do. This follows the same rule the game uses when deciding whether to put clothes on a prisoner.
[*]New mod setting, Keep colonists decent, on by default. Turn it off and none of the above applies: a stand will do exactly what its settings say, for everyone. It is there for colonies this would otherwise fight.
[/list]
